This folder contains code and data from Evans' PolRadTran RTM.

It has been extracted from the original PolRadTran tar and restructured.
If original code is modified, keep a copy of the original (as *.orig).

The original distribution is https://nit.coloradolinux.com/polrad.html
(PolRadTran.tar, sha256 7b0eff794319330321e27a6f312588a289ed080bb266500dcecf485f6a7cff9d).
It is distributed under the MIT licence in LICENSE, which must be kept with the
code.

Contents:

- radmat.f: Evans' matrix routines, used by both RT4 and RT3 and built once
  as the library polradtran_radmat.  It differs from the tar only by the
  rt4_ prefix on its BLAS helpers (rt4_daxpy, rt4_dscal, rt4_idamax,
  rt4_dswap), made in ARTS 2.  It keeps no state between calls; it is
  compiled with -frecursive (GNU) or -auto (Intel) so that MINVERT's local
  arrays are on the stack, because RT4 and RT3 serialise their calls with
  separate mutexes and may call it concurrently.
- rt4/: RT4 (horizontally oriented particles, thermal source, I and Q),
  as modified for ARTS 2.6.  The rt4/*.orig files and rt4/rt4.f are
  byte-identical to the tar.  Only the code needed to run RT4 is kept (no
  RT3-to-RT4 scattering data conversion, test data or run scripts).
- rt3/: RT3 (randomly oriented particles, solar and thermal sources, all
  Fourier azimuth modes, I, Q, U and V), new in ARTS 3.  rt3/*.orig,
  rt3/rt3.f, rt3/runmietest and rt3/runtesta are byte-identical to the tar;
  the two scripts hold Evans' expected benchmark outputs, which the ARTS
  tests compare with.  See rt3/README.

ARTS3 changes to RT4 (each marked with a "c ARTS3:" comment in the source):

- rt4/radutil4.f PLANCK_FUNCTION: the 5-digit radiation constants 1.1911D8
  and 1.4388D4 (a ~3e-5 relative bias, ~8 mK at 250 K) are replaced by 2hc^2
  [W m-2 sr-1 um^4] and hc/k [um K] evaluated from the exact SI (CODATA 2018)
  h, c and k.
- rt4/radtran4.f RADTRANO: NUUMMU is declared INTEGER (it was implicitly
  typed), and UP_RAD/DOWN_RAD are declared with their written extent
  NSTOKES*NUMMU*(NUM_LAYERS+1).
- rt4/rt4_c_interface.f90 (new): ISO_C_BINDING entry points with explicit C
  types for RADTRANO, PLANCK_FUNCTION and the three quadratures, so the build
  needs neither -fdefault-integer-8 nor the hidden CHARACTER length ABI.
- rt4/CMakeLists.txt: rewritten for ARTS3 (ENABLE_RT4).  rt4.f and the
  *.orig files are not built.  radmat.f moved from rt4/ to this folder
  (unchanged) when RT3 was added.

Nothing else is changed in RT4; in particular SYMMETRIC stays .TRUE., so RT4
only handles media that are mirror symmetric between the two hemispheres.
The C++ wrapper is src/core/rt4.

The ARTS3 changes to RT3 are listed in rt3/README; its C++ wrapper is
src/core/rt3.  CMakeLists.txt here enables the two with ENABLE_RT4 and
ENABLE_RT3; the legacy *.f files of both are compiled with
-std=legacy -fdefault-real-8 -fdefault-double-8 (GNU) or -r8 (Intel).
